\mt1 THE ACTS OF THE APOSTLES  
\c 8  
\p
\v 1 \w And\w* \w Saul\w* \w was\w* consenting \w unto\w* \w his\w* \w death\w*. \w And\w* \w at\w* \w that\w* \w time\w* there \w was\w* a \w great\w* \w persecution\w* \w against\w* the \w church\w* which \w was\w* \w at\w* \w Jerusalem\w*; \w and\w* they \w were\w* \w all\w* scattered \w abroad\w* \w throughout\w* the \w regions\w* of \w Judæa\w* \w and\w* \w Samaria\w*, \w except\w* the \w apostles\w*.  
\v 2 \w And\w* \w devout\w* \w men\w* \w carried\w* \w Stephen\w* \add to his burial\add*, \w and\w* \w made\w* \w great\w* \w lamentation\w* \w over\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 3 \w As\w* for \w Saul\w*, he made \w havock\w* of the \w church\w*, entering \w into\w* \w every\w* \w house\w*, \w and\w* \w haling\w* \w men\w* \w and\w* \w women\w* \w committed\w* \add them\add* \w to\w* \w prison\w*.  
\v 4 \w Therefore\w* \w they\w* that were scattered \w abroad\w* went every \w where\w* \w preaching\w* the \w word\w*.  
\v 5 \w Then\w* \w Philip\w* went \w down\w* \w to\w* the \w city\w* of \w Samaria\w*, and \w preached\w* \w Christ\w* unto \w them\w*.  
\v 6 \w And\w* the \w people\w* \w with\w* one \w accord\w* gave \w heed\w* \w unto\w* those \w things\w* \w which\w* \w Philip\w* \w spake\w*, \w hearing\w* \w and\w* \w seeing\w* the \w miracles\w* \w which\w* he \w did\w*.  
\v 7 \w For\w* \w unclean\w* \w spirits\w*, \w crying\w* with \w loud\w* \w voice\w*, came \w out\w* of \w many\w* that were \w possessed\w* \add with them\add*: \w and\w* \w many\w* taken with \w palsies\w*, \w and\w* that \w were\w* \w lame\w*, were \w healed\w*.  
\v 8 \w And\w* there \w was\w* \w great\w* \w joy\w* \w in\w* \w that\w* \w city\w*.  
\v 9 But there \w was\w* a \w certain\w* \w man\w*, \w called\w* \w Simon\w*, which \w beforetime\w* \w in\w* the same \w city\w* used \w sorcery\w*, \w and\w* \w bewitched\w* the \w people\w* of \w Samaria\w*, giving out \w that\w* \w himself\w* \w was\w* \w some\w* great \w one\w*:  
\v 10 To \w whom\w* they \w all\w* gave \w heed\w*, \w from\w* the \w least\w* \w to\w* the \w greatest\w*, \w saying\w*, This \w man\w* \w is\w* the \w great\w* \w power\w* of \w God\w*.  
\v 11 \w And\w* to \w him\w* they had \w regard\w*, because \w that\w* of \w long\w* \w time\w* he had \w bewitched\w* \w them\w* with \w sorceries\w*.  
\v 12 \w But\w* \w when\w* they \w believed\w* \w Philip\w* \w preaching\w* the \w things\w* \w concerning\w* the \w kingdom\w* of \w God\w*, \w and\w* the \w name\w* of \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w*, they were \w baptized\w*, \w both\w* \w men\w* \w and\w* \w women\w*.  
\v 13 \w Then\w* \w Simon\w* \w himself\w* \w believed\w* \w also\w*: \w and\w* when he \w was\w* \w baptized\w*, he \w continued\w* with \w Philip\w*, \w and\w* \w wondered\w*, \w beholding\w* the \w miracles\w* \w and\w* \w signs\w* which were \w done\w*.  
\v 14 Now \w when\w* the \w apostles\w* which \w were\w* \w at\w* \w Jerusalem\w* \w heard\w* \w that\w* \w Samaria\w* had \w received\w* the \w word\w* of \w God\w*, they \w sent\w* \w unto\w* \w them\w* \w Peter\w* \w and\w* \w John\w*:  
\v 15 \w Who\w*, when they were come \w down\w*, \w prayed\w* \w for\w* \w them\w*, \w that\w* they might \w receive\w* the \w Holy\w* \w Ghost\w*:  
\v 16 (\w For\w* as \w yet\w* he \w was\w* \w fallen\w* \w upon\w* \w none\w* of \w them\w*: \w only\w* they \w were\w* \w baptized\w* \w in\w* the \w name\w* of the \w Lord\w* \w Jesus\w*.)  
\v 17 \w Then\w* laid \w they\w* \add their\add* \w hands\w* \w on\w* \w them\w*, \w and\w* they \w received\w* the \w Holy\w* \w Ghost\w*.  
\v 18 \w And\w* when \w Simon\w* \w saw\w* \w that\w* \w through\w* laying \w on\w* of the \w apostles’\w* \w hands\w* the \w Holy\w* \w Ghost\w* was \w given\w*, he \w offered\w* \w them\w* \w money\w*,  
\v 19 \w Saying\w*, Give \w me\w* \w also\w* \w this\w* \w power\w*, \w that\w* on \w whomsoever\w* I \w lay\w* \w hands\w*, he may \w receive\w* the \w Holy\w* \w Ghost\w*.  
\v 20 \w But\w* \w Peter\w* \w said\w* \w unto\w* \w him\w*, \w Thy\w* \w money\w* \w perish\w* \w with\w* \w thee\w*, \w because\w* thou hast \w thought\w* \w that\w* the \w gift\w* of \w God\w* may be \w purchased\w* with \w money\w*.  
\v 21 \w Thou\w* \w hast\w* \w neither\w* \w part\w* \w nor\w* \w lot\w* \w in\w* \w this\w* \w matter\w*: \w for\w* \w thy\w* \w heart\w* \w is\w* \w not\w* \w right\w* in the sight \w of\w* \w God\w*.  
\v 22 \w Repent\w* \w therefore\w* \w of\w* \w this\w* \w thy\w* \w wickedness\w*, \w and\w* \w pray\w* \w God\w*, \w if\w* \w perhaps\w* the \w thought\w* of \w thine\w* \w heart\w* may be \w forgiven\w* \w thee\w*.  
\v 23 \w For\w* I \w perceive\w* that \w thou\w* \w art\w* \w in\w* the \w gall\w* of \w bitterness\w*, \w and\w* \add in\add* the \w bond\w* of \w iniquity\w*.  
\v 24 \w Then\w* \w answered\w* \w Simon\w*, and \w said\w*, \w Pray\w* \w ye\w* \w to\w* the \w Lord\w* \w for\w* \w me\w*, \w that\w* none of these \w things\w* \w which\w* ye have \w spoken\w* \w come\w* \w upon\w* \w me\w*.  
\v 25 \w And\w* \w they\w*, when they had \w testified\w* \w and\w* \w preached\w* the \w word\w* of the \w Lord\w*, \w returned\w* \w to\w* \w Jerusalem\w*, \w and\w* preached the \w gospel\w* in \w many\w* \w villages\w* of the \w Samaritans\w*.  
\v 26 \w And\w* the \w angel\w* of the \w Lord\w* \w spake\w* \w unto\w* \w Philip\w*, \w saying\w*, \w Arise\w*, \w and\w* \w go\w* \w toward\w* the \w south\w* \w unto\w* the \w way\w* \w that\w* goeth \w down\w* \w from\w* \w Jerusalem\w* \w unto\w* \w Gaza\w*, \w which\w* \w is\w* \w desert\w*.  
\v 27 \w And\w* he \w arose\w* and \w went\w*: \w and\w*, \w behold\w*, a \w man\w* of \w Ethiopia\w*, an \w eunuch\w* of great \w authority\w* under \w Candace\w* \w queen\w* of the \w Ethiopians\w*, \w who\w* \w had\w* the charge \w of\w* \w all\w* \w her\w* \w treasure\w*, and had \w come\w* \w to\w* \w Jerusalem\w* for to \w worship\w*,  
\v 28 \w Was\w* \w returning\w*, \w and\w* \w sitting\w* \w in\w* \w his\w* \w chariot\w* \w read\w* \w Esaias\w* the \w prophet\w*.  
\v 29 \w Then\w* the \w Spirit\w* \w said\w* unto \w Philip\w*, Go \w near\w*, \w and\w* join \w thyself\w* to \w this\w* \w chariot\w*.  
\v 30 \w And\w* \w Philip\w* ran \w thither\w* to \add him\add*, and \w heard\w* \w him\w* \w read\w* the \w prophet\w* \w Esaias\w*, \w and\w* \w said\w*, Understandest \w thou\w* \w what\w* thou \w readest\w*?  
\v 31 \w And\w* he \w said\w*, \w How\w* can \w I\w*, \w except\w* some \w man\w* should \w guide\w* \w me\w*? \w And\w* he \w desired\w* \w Philip\w* that he would come \w up\w* and \w sit\w* \w with\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 32 The \w place\w* of the \w scripture\w* \w which\w* he \w read\w* \w was\w* \w this\w*, He was \w led\w* \w as\w* a \w sheep\w* \w to\w* the \w slaughter\w*; \w and\w* \w like\w* a \w lamb\w* \w dumb\w* \w before\w* \w his\w* \w shearer\w*, \w so\w* opened \w he\w* \w not\w* \w his\w* \w mouth\w*:  
\v 33 \w In\w* \w his\w* \w humiliation\w* \w his\w* \w judgment\w* was taken \w away\w*: \w and\w* \w who\w* shall \w declare\w* \w his\w* \w generation\w*? \w for\w* \w his\w* \w life\w* is \w taken\w* \w from\w* the \w earth\w*.  
\v 34 \w And\w* the \w eunuch\w* \w answered\w* \w Philip\w*, and \w said\w*, I \w pray\w* \w thee\w*, \w of\w* \w whom\w* \w speaketh\w* the \w prophet\w* \w this\w*? \w of\w* \w himself\w*, \w or\w* \w of\w* \w some\w* other \w man\w*?  
\v 35 \w Then\w* \w Philip\w* \w opened\w* \w his\w* \w mouth\w*, \w and\w* \w began\w* \w at\w* the \w same\w* \w scripture\w*, and \w preached\w* unto \w him\w* \w Jesus\w*.  
\v 36 \w And\w* \w as\w* they \w went\w* \w on\w* \add their\add* \w way\w*, they \w came\w* \w unto\w* a \w certain\w* \w water\w*: \w and\w* the \w eunuch\w* \w said\w*, \w See\w*, \add here is\add* \w water\w*; \w what\w* doth \w hinder\w* \w me\w* to be \w baptized\w*?  
\v 37 \w And\w* \w Philip\w* \w said\w*, \w If\w* thou \w believest\w* \w with\w* \w all\w* thine \w heart\w*, thou \w mayest\w*. And he \w answered\w* \w and\w* \w said\w*, I \w believe\w* that \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w* \w is\w* the \w Son\w* of \w God\w*.  
\v 38 \w And\w* he \w commanded\w* the \w chariot\w* to stand \w still\w*: \w and\w* they went \w down\w* \w both\w* \w into\w* the \w water\w*, \w both\w* \w Philip\w* \w and\w* the \w eunuch\w*; \w and\w* he \w baptized\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 39 \w And\w* \w when\w* they were come \w up\w* out \w of\w* the \w water\w*, the \w Spirit\w* of the \w Lord\w* caught \w away\w* \w Philip\w*, \w that\w* the \w eunuch\w* \w saw\w* \w him\w* no \w more\w*: \w and\w* he \w went\w* on \w his\w* \w way\w* \w rejoicing\w*.  
\v 40 \w But\w* \w Philip\w* was \w found\w* \w at\w* \w Azotus\w*: \w and\w* passing \w through\w* he \w preached\w* in \w all\w* the \w cities\w*, \w till\w* \w he\w* \w came\w* \w to\w* \w Cæsarea\w*.
